# data/ — the data root (never commit state; README is the law doc)
# ONE rule: ignore everything under data/, then re-include directory
# traversal (so .gitkeep discovery works) and the law doc. The old
# per-subdir list + a trailing !data/**/ negation broke itself —
# dir-only ignores lose to the later dir negation, git descended, and
# NO pattern matched any file: everything under data/ was committable,
# llm_keystore.json/.key included. (-pattern lines were not gitignore
# syntax at all — dead text.)
data/**
!data/**/
!data/README.md
!data/**/.gitkeep
